{"text": " Orders don't arrive in neat forms. They come however your customers choose to send them. A WhatsApp message, a voice note, a handwritten list photographed on a phone, an email. Everyone looks different. Everyone still needs to become an actual order. And today, that usually means someone on your team has to read it, understand it, then type everything in by hand. Meet Maya. Instead of starting from scratch, your team simply forwards the order to Maya, right where they already work. WhatsApp. Maya reads the message, listens to the voice note, reads the handwritten list, then starts making sense of what the customer actually ordered. It matches every item to the right SKU, the right unit, and the price you've agreed with that customer. A messy WhatsApp order becomes clean, structured information your team can actually work with. From there, Maya helps prepare the quotation, the sales order, the delivery order, and the invoice. Same order, same details. No need to keep retyping the same information from one document to the next. Your team stays in control. They review it, correct anything that needs correcting, and confirm before it goes through. Then everything syncs back to your business system, whether you're using SQL account, auto-count, or your connected ERP. So WhatsApp and your order system finally work together. Maya lives in WhatsApp, turns messy orders into structured work, and syncs them back to your system. Start at maya.whatsapp.my. Do not try. Do not try. Do not try.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 2.26, "text": " Orders don't arrive in neat forms.", "tokens": [50365, 1610, 15633, 500, 380, 8881, 294, 10654, 6422, 13, 50481], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.2153424644470215, "compression_ratio": 1.5537190082644627, "no_speech_prob": 4.8828263481126566e-12, "words": [{"word": " Orders", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.48, "probability": 0.70458984375}, {"word": " don't", "start": 0.48, "end": 0.9, "probability": 0.99511718